# CVE-2026-32933 (GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x) — AutoMapper 14.0.0 DoS via
# uncontrolled recursion, detected in the API/migrator image .deps.json.
# AutoMapper is pinned by ABP Framework 9 (Volo.Abp.AutoMapper): the fixed
# versions (15.1.1/16.1.1) are a major upgrade that ABP 9.3.x cannot load at
# runtime (MissingMethodException; verified incident, see common.props).
# Risk assessment: mapping profiles only map bounded internal DTOs;
# attacker-controlled object graphs are depth-limited by System.Text.Json
# (MaxDepth=64) before mapping and recursive profiles are capped MaxDepth(8).
# Owner: backend team (docs/43-dependency-security-policy.md, doc 08 B-6).
# Remove together with the common.props pin/suppression and the
# Test-NuGetVulnerabilities.ps1 allow-list entry when the ABP 10 upgrade
# lands. Expiration enforced below: the scan fails again after this date so
# the exception must be consciously renewed or removed.
CVE-2026-32933 exp:2026-12-31
